IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `ip-nouns`
IMPORT `ip-framework`
IMPORT `ip-rule-of-reason`
IMPORT `ip-restraints`
IMPORT `ip-safety-zone`

-- Antitrust Guidelines for the Licensing of Intellectual Property (2017) -- tests of the
-- thresholds and branches, from the text of each rule. Both sides of every threshold;
-- every branch; one discriminating fixture per fork (NOTES.md section 8 names the forks
-- that have none), which is the case where the reading chosen and its alternative give
-- different answers.
--
-- No numbered Example applies the safety zone (4.3) with figures, so its fixtures are
-- constructed from 4.3's own words. Market shares are percent points.
--
-- A failing assertion is a finding: no expected value was edited to match the code. On
-- review (2026-11-25) four readings were revised and their assertions with them, each
-- marked "revised on review" where it stands: F8 (n.85 and the zone), F16 (blocked wins;
-- a clear alternative wins), 5.1's own words, and section 6's inequitable-conduct sentence.
-- Later the same day F23 and F24 gained their third value, and their assertions say so;
-- the F25 result names took the text's modal and voice, which respelled the 3.3, 5.2 and
-- 5.5 expected values with no reading changed, and 5.5's per se words were confined to
-- the two restraints it names (NOTES.md section 13).

§ `Thresholds and branches`

§§ `Fixtures`

`no transfer` MEANS `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

-- 3.2.2's three ways the rights may reach the market (fork F24).
`marketed separately` MEANS `the rights to the intellectual property are marketed separately from the products in which they are used`
`as an integral part of a marketed good` MEANS `the intellectual property is licensed, sold or transferred as an integral part of a marketed good`
`not stated how licensed` MEANS `how the intellectual property is licensed is not stated`

-- The agencies' three states of conclusion on a restraint's effect (fork F23).
`no likely effect` MEANS `the agencies conclude that the restraint is unlikely to have an anticompetitive effect`
`a likely effect` MEANS `the agencies conclude that the restraint has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect`
`no conclusion yet` MEANS `the agencies have not yet concluded on the restraint's anticompetitive effect`

`a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` MEANS `Restraint in a licensing arrangement` WITH
    `the type of restraint` IS `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment`
    `the restraint is of a kind that would always or almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices` IS FALSE
    `the restraint can be expected to contribute to an efficiency-enhancing integration of economic activity` IS TRUE
    `the restraint is reasonably related to efficiencies` IS TRUE

GIVEN kind IS A `Type of restraint`
      always IS A BOOLEAN
      integration IS A BOOLEAN
      related IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
`a restraint of` MEANS `Restraint in a licensing arrangement` WITH
    `the type of restraint` IS kind
    `the restraint is of a kind that would always or almost always tend to reduce output or increase prices` IS always
    `the restraint can be expected to contribute to an efficiency-enhancing integration of economic activity` IS integration
    `the restraint is reasonably related to efficiencies` IS related

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      controller IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other technology`
`an independent substitute technology` MEANS `Other technology` OF name, controller, FALSE, TRUE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other technology`
`a technology the parties control` MEANS `Other technology` OF name, "the licensor", TRUE, TRUE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other technology`
`a technology not substitutable at a comparable cost` MEANS `Other technology` OF name, name, FALSE, FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      controller IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other research and development entity`
`a capable entity controlled by` MEANS `Other research and development entity` OF name, controller, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other research and development entity`
`a capable entity the parties control` MEANS `Other research and development entity` OF name, "the licensor", TRUE, TRUE, TRUE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH AN `Other research and development entity`
`an entity without the incentive` MEANS `Other research and development entity` OF name, name, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      kind IS A `Kind of relevant market`
      licensor IS A NUMBER
      licensees IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`a market with share data` MEANS `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` WITH
    `the name of the market` IS name
    `the kind of market` IS kind
    `the parties' shares` IS JUST (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF licensor, licensees)
    `the other technologies` IS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T4" "C4"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T5" "C5")
    `the other entities` IS LIST (`a capable entity controlled by` "E1" "C1"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E2" "C2"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E3" "C3"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E4" "C4"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E5" "C5")

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      licensor IS A NUMBER
      licensees IS A LIST OF NUMBER
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`a goods market at` MEANS `a market with share data` name `a goods market` licensor licensees

GIVEN name IS A STRING
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`a goods market without share data` MEANS `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` OF name, `a goods market`, NOTHING, EMPTY, EMPTY

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      technologies IS A LIST OF `Other technology`
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`a technology market without share data` MEANS `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` OF name, `a technology market`, NOTHING, technologies, EMPTY

GIVEN name IS A STRING
      entities IS A LIST OF `Other research and development entity`
GIVETH A `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
`a research and development market without share data` MEANS `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint` OF name, `a research and development market`, NOTHING, EMPTY, entities

GIVEN form IS A `Form of intellectual property`
      inLicensing IS A BOOLEAN
      relatedToUse IS A BOOLEAN
      transfer IS A `Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)`
      restraint IS A `Restraint in a licensing arrangement`
      wider IS A BOOLEAN
      markets IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
`an arrangement` MEANS `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)` WITH
    `the form of the intellectual property licensed` IS form
    `the restraint is in a licensing arrangement` IS inLicensing
    `the restraint is related to the use of the licensed intellectual property` IS relatedToUse
    `the transfer` IS transfer
    `the restraint` IS restraint
    `the analysis of goods markets alone would inadequately address the effects of the arrangement on competition among technologies or in research and development` IS wider
    `the relevant markets significantly affected by the restraint` IS markets

-- The usual case: a patent license, the restraint in it and related to the use of the
-- patent, no transfer, a restraint not facially anticompetitive.
GIVEN wider IS A BOOLEAN
      markets IS A LIST OF `Relevant market significantly affected by the restraint`
GIVETH A `Licensing arrangement before the safety zone (4.3)`
`a patent license affecting` MEANS `an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` wider markets

`inside` MEANS JUST `inside the safety zone: absent extraordinary circumstances, the agencies will not challenge the restraint`

GIVEN names IS A LIST OF STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE `Safety zone result (4.3)`
`outside, for the markets` MEANS JUST (`outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside` (`a relevant market significantly affected by the restraint does not meet its criterion` names))

`outside, as facially anticompetitive` MEANS JUST (`outside the safety zone: the agencies will analyze the arrangement on the considerations of parts 3 to 5, and it is not anticompetitive merely for being outside` `the restraint is facially anticompetitive`)

`four independent technologies` MEANS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T4" "C4")
`three independent technologies` MEANS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3")

§§ `4.3 condition (2): twenty percent, both sides`

-- 12 + 5 + 3 = 20: "no more than twenty percent" includes exactly twenty.
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 12, LIST 5, 3) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 12 (LIST 5, 3))) EQUALS `inside`
-- 12 + 5 + 3.01 = 20.01: outside, naming the market.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 12 (LIST 5, 3.01))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widgets")
-- The licensor alone at 20 and at 20.01.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 20 EMPTY)) EQUALS `inside`
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 20.01 EMPTY)) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widgets")

-- Fork F1 (assumed, not ruled): "collectively account for" is the SUM of the parties' own
-- shares. Licensor 15 and one licensee 10, each under twenty alone: outside, at 25.
-- (Reading the limit per party would put this inside.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 15, LIST 10) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 15 (LIST 10))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widgets")

-- Impossible shares: a sum over 100, a share over 100, a negative share. NOTHING.
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 60, LIST 50) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 101, EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 10, LIST (0 MINUS 5)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 60 (LIST 50))) EQUALS NOTHING
-- 100 is possible (a sole licensor and licensee with the whole market), and outside.
#ASSERT `4.3: the share the licensor and its licensees collectively account for` (`Market shares of the licensor and its licensees` OF 100, LIST 0) EQUALS JUST 100

§§ `4.3 condition (2): each relevant market significantly affected`

-- Fork F2 (assumed, not ruled): EACH market considered must meet its criterion. Two goods
-- markets at 15 and 21: outside, naming only the second. (Reading the limit as met when
-- any one market meets it would put this inside.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 15 EMPTY), (`a goods market at` "gadgets" 21 EMPTY))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "gadgets")
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 15 EMPTY), (`a goods market at` "gadgets" 20 EMPTY))) EQUALS `inside`
-- Two failing markets are both named, in the order given.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 30 EMPTY), (`a goods market at` "gadgets" 21 EMPTY))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widgets", "gadgets")

-- Fork F7 (assumed, not ruled): a goods market without usable share data has no criterion
-- in the text: NOTHING. Alone: NOTHING. With a passing market: NOTHING. With a failing
-- market: outside, on the failing market alone.
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a goods market without share data` "widgets") EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a goods market without share data` "widgets")) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market without share data` "widgets"), (`a goods market at` "gadgets" 10 EMPTY))) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market without share data` "widgets"), (`a goods market at` "gadgets" 25 EMPTY))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "gadgets")

-- Fork F10 (assumed, not ruled): no market to consider: NOTHING.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE EMPTY) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `4.3: goods markets only, unless`

-- "by reference only to goods markets unless ...": a failing technology market is not
-- considered when goods-market analysis is adequate; it is when it is not.
`a passing goods market and a failing technology market` MEANS LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 15 EMPTY), (`a technology market without share data` "widget technology" `three independent technologies`)

#ASSERT `4.3: the markets by reference to which the safety zone is determined` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE `a passing goods market and a failing technology market`) EQUALS LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 15 EMPTY)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE `a passing goods market and a failing technology market`) EQUALS `inside`
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE `a passing goods market and a failing technology market`) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widget technology")
-- Only technology markets, goods-market analysis adequate: nothing to consider (F10).
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST `a technology market without share data` "widget technology" `four independent technologies`)) EQUALS NOTHING

-- Fork F15 (assumed, not ruled): when goods-market analysis alone is inadequate, every
-- listed market is considered, goods markets included. A goods market at 25 and a
-- technology market without share data with four independent technologies: outside, on
-- the goods market. (Considering only the technology and research and development
-- markets would put this inside.)
`a failing goods market and a passing technology market` MEANS LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 25 EMPTY), (`a technology market without share data` "widget technology" `four independent technologies`)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE `a failing goods market and a passing technology market`) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "widgets")

-- Fork F27 (assumed, not ruled): a share is checked only in a market the zone considers.
-- A technology market at an impossible 500 is passed over when goods-market analysis is
-- adequate. (Refusing any impossible share anywhere would answer NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` FALSE (LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 10 EMPTY), (`a market with share data` "widget technology" `a technology market` 500 EMPTY))) EQUALS `inside`

§§ `4.3: technology markets without share data -- four or more`

#ASSERT `the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` `four independent technologies` EQUALS 4
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a technology market without share data` "T" `four independent technologies`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a technology market without share data` "T" `three independent technologies`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a technology market without share data` "T" `four independent technologies`)) EQUALS `inside`
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a technology market without share data` "T" `three independent technologies`)) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "T")

-- Fork F3 (assumed, not ruled): "independently controlled" counts controllers. Four
-- technologies, two of them controlled by one firm: three. (Counting technologies would
-- give four, and inside.)
`four technologies, three controllers` MEANS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T4" "C3")
#ASSERT `the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` `four technologies, three controllers` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a technology market without share data` "T" `four technologies, three controllers`)) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "T")

-- "in addition to the technologies controlled by the parties": a party's technology does
-- not count. Nor does one that is not substitutable at a comparable cost.
`three independent, one of the parties', one not substitutable` MEANS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3"), (`a technology the parties control` "P1"), (`a technology not substitutable at a comparable cost` "X1")
#ASSERT `the number of independently controlled technologies in addition to those of the parties that may be substitutable at a comparable cost` `three independent, one of the parties', one not substitutable` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a technology market without share data` "T" `three independent, one of the parties', one not substitutable`) EQUALS JUST FALSE

-- The two counts the guidelines give for a technology market do not agree, and are not
-- mixed. Two technologies of the parties and four others, comparably efficient, no share
-- data: 3.2.2 "will assign" each of the six the same share, 100/6 percent, so the parties'
-- two have about 33 percent; the safety zone's own criterion for a technology market
-- without share data counts the four others and puts it inside.
`six comparably efficient technologies, no share data` MEANS `Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, TRUE, 6
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` `six comparably efficient technologies, no share data` EQUALS JUST (100 DIVIDED BY 6)
`four independent technologies and two of the parties'` MEANS LIST (`an independent substitute technology` "T1" "C1"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T2" "C2"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T3" "C3"), (`an independent substitute technology` "T4" "C4"), (`a technology the parties control` "P1"), (`a technology the parties control` "P2")
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a technology market without share data` "T" `four independent technologies and two of the parties'`)) EQUALS `inside`

-- Fork F6 (assumed, not ruled): with accurate share data, a technology market is tested at
-- twenty percent like a goods market, whatever the count. At 18: inside; at 25 with five
-- independent technologies: outside. (Applying the count whenever four exist would put the
-- second inside.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a market with share data` "T" `a technology market` 18 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a market with share data` "T" `a technology market` 25 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 10 EMPTY), (`a market with share data` "T" `a technology market` 25 EMPTY))) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "T")

§§ `4.3: research and development markets without share data -- four or more`

`four capable entities` MEANS LIST (`a capable entity controlled by` "E1" "C1"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E2" "C2"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E3" "C3"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E4" "C4")
`three capable entities` MEANS LIST (`a capable entity controlled by` "E1" "C1"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E2" "C2"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E3" "C3")
-- Two subsidiaries of one parent, a party's own laboratory, and one without the incentive.
`four entities that count as three` MEANS LIST (`a capable entity controlled by` "E1" "C1"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E2" "C2"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E3a" "C3"), (`a capable entity controlled by` "E3b" "C3"), (`a capable entity the parties control` "lab"), (`an entity without the incentive` "E5")

#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a research and development market without share data` "R" `four capable entities`) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a research and development market without share data` "R" `three capable entities`) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `the number of independently controlled entities in addition to the parties that possess the required assets and the incentive` `four entities that count as three` EQUALS 3
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a research and development market without share data` "R" `four capable entities`)) EQUALS `inside`
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`a patent license affecting` TRUE (LIST `a research and development market without share data` "R" `four entities that count as three`)) EQUALS `outside, for the markets` (LIST "R")
-- With share data, a research and development market is tested at twenty percent (F6).
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a market with share data` "R" `a research and development market` 20 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `4.3: the market meets its criterion` (`a market with share data` "R" `a research and development market` 21 EMPTY) EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- Fork F13 (assumed, not ruled): Example 3's screen and 4.3's criterion use the same count.
#ASSERT `Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` `four entities that count as three` NOTHING EQUALS JUST `the agency would consider whether the joint venture would give the parties an incentive and ability collectively to reduce investment in, or otherwise to retard the pace or scope of, research and development`
-- Example 3's last branch it does not answer: fewer than four and no significant risk.
#ASSERT `Example 3: the screen for a research and development joint venture` `three capable entities` (JUST FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `4.3 condition (1): facially anticompetitive`

-- A per se type at a five percent share: outside.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 5 EMPTY)) EQUALS `outside, as facially anticompetitive`
-- Fork F27 (assumed, not ruled): condition (1) comes before the shares, so a per se
-- restraint is outside even beside an impossible share of 150. (Refusing impossible
-- shares first would answer NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 150 EMPTY)) EQUALS `outside, as facially anticompetitive`
-- A type not per se, but of a kind that would always or almost always reduce output or
-- raise prices (n.59, second limb): outside.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE TRUE TRUE) FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 5 EMPTY)) EQUALS `outside, as facially anticompetitive`
-- Fork F4 (assumed, not ruled): facially anticompetitive by type, whatever the
-- integration. Market division that contributes to an efficiency-enhancing integration is
-- judged under the rule of reason (3.4), and is still outside the zone (n.59 "restraints
-- that normally warrant per se treatment"). (Reading n.59 through 3.4's mode would put it
-- inside.)
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` (`a restraint of` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE TRUE TRUE) FALSE (LIST `a goods market at` "widgets" 5 EMPTY)) EQUALS `outside, as facially anticompetitive`
#ASSERT NOT `4.3: the restraint is facially anticompetitive` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive`

§§ `4.3: where the safety zone does not apply`

`one small goods market` MEANS LIST (`a goods market at` "widgets" 5 EMPTY)

-- n.58.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` FALSE TRUE `no transfer` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the restraint is not in a licensing arrangement`)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE FALSE `no transfer` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the restraint is unrelated to the use of the licensed intellectual property`)
-- 4.3, n.86, 5.7: an outright sale, and an exclusive license.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the agencies apply a merger analysis to the transfer`)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the agencies apply a merger analysis to the transfer`)
-- Fork F8 (assumed, not ruled; revised on review 2026-11-25): a license that only in
-- substance transfers the rights, to which the agencies "may also apply" a merger
-- analysis (n.85), is one of the transfers "such as those described in this section"
-- (n.86): the zone does not apply, for that reason. (Reading n.86 as covering only the
-- sale and the exclusive license would leave it NOTHING, or inside; the earlier reading
-- here was NOTHING.)
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` TRUE TRUE (`Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the transfer is one of those described in section 5.7 (n.86), to which the agencies may also apply a merger analysis (n.85)`)
-- 1.0, n.1: a trademark license is outside these guidelines (fork F14): NOTHING. A mask
-- work is treated as a copyright (n.8): the zone is applied.
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a trademark` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a mask work fixed in a semiconductor chip product` TRUE TRUE `no transfer` `a restraint that is not facially anticompetitive` FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS `inside`
-- The n.58 gate comes before condition (1): a per se restraint outside any licensing
-- arrangement is "does not apply", not "outside".
#ASSERT `4.3: the antitrust safety zone` (`an arrangement` `a patent` FALSE TRUE `no transfer` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) FALSE `one small goods market`) EQUALS JUST (`the safety zone does not apply` `the restraint is not in a licensing arrangement`)

§§ `1.0 and 2.1`

#ASSERT `1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a trademark` EQUALS `not covered: these guidelines do not cover the antitrust treatment of trademarks`
#ASSERT `1.0: whether the guidelines cover licensing of` `a mask work fixed in a semiconductor chip product` EQUALS `covered by these guidelines`
#ASSERT `2.1: the reach of the principles` (`Determinations on the reach of the antitrust laws (2.1)` OF TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the principles of these guidelines apply equally to all licensing arrangements`
#ASSERT `2.1: the reach of the principles` (`Determinations on the reach of the antitrust laws (2.1)` OF TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `2.1: the reach of the principles` (`Determinations on the reach of the antitrust laws (2.1)` OF FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `3.1`

#ASSERT `3.1: when competition among actual or potential competitors may be adversely affected` (LIST `facilitating market division`, `facilitating price-fixing`) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will follow the analysis set forth in sections 3.2 to 5`

§§ `3.2.2 and 3.2.3`

-- Fork F24 (assumed, not ruled; revised 2026-11-25): three ways the rights may reach the
-- market. Marketed separately: "may analyze"; licensed as an integral part of a marketed
-- good: n.33's "no need"; not stated: NOTHING. (The earlier reading gave a caller who had
-- not said n.33's answer; the third assertion is the case it answered differently.)
#ASSERT `3.2.2: whether a technology market is analysed` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, TRUE, TRUE, 3) EQUALS JUST `the agencies may analyse the competitive effects of the arrangement in a technology market`
#ASSERT `3.2.2: whether a technology market is analysed` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `as an integral part of a marketed good`, TRUE, TRUE, 3) EQUALS JUST `there is no need for a separate analysis of technology markets`
#ASSERT `3.2.2: whether a technology market is analysed` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `not stated how licensed`, TRUE, TRUE, 3) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Where the rule above does not say a technology market may be analysed, no share is
-- assigned in one (revised on review 2026-11-25).
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `as an integral part of a marketed good`, FALSE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `not stated how licensed`, FALSE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The equal share "will assign": both conditions and a whole count of at least one.
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS JUST 20
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, TRUE, 1) EQUALS JUST 100
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, TRUE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, FALSE, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, TRUE, 0) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the market share the agencies will assign to each technology` (`Technology-market facts (3.2.2)` OF `marketed separately`, FALSE, TRUE, 3.5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Fork F16 (assumed, not ruled; revised on review 2026-11-25): a technology said to be a
-- substitute and blocked at once is blocked, and the parties are not actual competitors
-- in it (Example 9: blocking patents "are not substitutable"). (The earlier reading here
-- was NOTHING; letting substitution win would answer TRUE.)
#ASSERT `3.2.2: the parties are actual competitors in the technology market` (`Two parties' technologies (3.2.2)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST FALSE

#ASSERT `3.2.3: whether a research and development market is analysed` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not delineate a research and development market`
#ASSERT `3.2.3: whether a research and development market is analysed` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not delineate a research and development market`
#ASSERT `3.2.3: whether a research and development market is analysed` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, 5) EQUALS NOTHING
-- The equal share "may assign".
#ASSERT `3.2.3: the equal market share the agencies may assign to each entity` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 4) EQUALS JUST 25
#ASSERT `3.2.3: the equal market share the agencies may assign to each entity` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, 4) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `3.2.3: the equal market share the agencies may assign to each entity` (`Research and development facts (3.2.3)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, 0) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `3.3`

#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` OF "M", FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS `no horizontal or vertical component`
-- A potential competitor (n.27) is enough for a horizontal component.
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` OF "M", FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies ordinarily will treat the relationship as having a horizontal component`
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship of the parties in the market` (`Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` OF "M", FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS `a vertical relationship, which the agencies ordinarily will treat as also having a horizontal component`
#ASSERT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` OF "M", FALSE, TRUE, TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT `3.3: the relationship has a horizontal component` (`Two parties in a relevant market (3.3)` OF "M", FALSE, FALSE, TRUE)

§§ `3.4 and 5.1`

#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `an output restraint` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `a group boycott of a kind accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
-- Fork F5 (assumed, not ruled): 3.4's list is open; a type the caller classes as accorded
-- per se treatment is treated like the named ones.
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `another type of restraint accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
#ASSERT `3.4: the mode of analysis` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`

`the finding of no likely effect` MEANS `Findings under the rule of reason` OF `no likely effect`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`no finding` MEANS `Findings under the rule of reason` OF `no conclusion yet`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE) `the finding of no likely effect` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will treat the restraint as reasonable, without an elaborate analysis of market power or the justifications for it`
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE) `no finding` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will likely challenge the restraint without an elaborate analysis of particular industry circumstances`
-- Facially of that kind, but reasonably related to efficiencies: the full inquiry.
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE TRUE TRUE) `no finding` EQUALS JUST `the agencies inquire into the likely competitive effects, in an inquiry meet for the case, as in part 4`
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE) `no finding` EQUALS JUST `the agencies inquire into the likely competitive effects, in an inquiry meet for the case, as in part 4`
-- Fork F23 (assumed, not ruled): 3.4 reads only the conclusion of no likely effect; a
-- contrary conclusion leaves the inquiry to part 4, as no conclusion does.
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` FALSE TRUE TRUE) (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies inquire into the likely competitive effects, in an inquiry meet for the case, as in part 4`
-- Contradictory findings: no likely effect, and facially always harmful with no related
-- efficiency. NOTHING.
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `a type of restraint not accorded per se treatment` TRUE FALSE FALSE) `the finding of no likely effect` EQUALS NOTHING
-- The per se mode wins over any rule-of-reason finding.
#ASSERT `3.4: what the agencies do with the restraint` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) `the finding of no likely effect` EQUALS JUST `the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule, without an elaborate inquiry into its likely competitive effect`
-- 5.1 in its own words (revised on review 2026-11-25; it returned 3.4's "will challenge").
#ASSERT `5.1: the mode of analysis of a horizontal restraint` (`a restraint of` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the restraint may merit per se treatment`
#ASSERT `5.1: the mode of analysis of a horizontal restraint` (`a restraint of` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `following section 3.4, the agencies will evaluate the restraint under the rule of reason`

§§ `4.1.1`

#ASSERT `4.1.1: the considerations bearing on the risk of harm that are present` (`Market characteristics (4.1.1, 5.4)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS LIST `concentration of the relevant markets`, `difficulty of entry`, `low responsiveness of supply and demand to changes in price`, `a large proportion of the relevant markets affected by the restraint`, `the long duration of the restraint`, `similar restraints imposed by owners of competing technologies`, `common restraints on competing licensees`
#ASSERT `4.1.1: the considerations bearing on the risk of harm that are present` (`Market characteristics (4.1.1, 5.4)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS LIST `difficulty of entry`, `the long duration of the restraint`

§§ `4.1.2`

GIVEN byTerms IS A BOOLEAN
      byStructure IS A BOOLEAN
      dealingTerm IS A BOOLEAN
      dealingCost IS A BOOLEAN
      other IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `License terms and structure (4.1.2)`
`a license where` MEANS `License terms and structure (4.1.2)` OF byTerms, byStructure, dealingTerm, dealingCost, other, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE

`no horizontal relationship` MEANS `Horizontal relationships among the parties (4.1.2)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE
`licensees in a horizontal relationship` MEANS `Horizontal relationships among the parties (4.1.2)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE

-- Exclusive in effect though not in form.
#ASSERT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive licensing` (`a license where` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT `4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`a license where` FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `no horizontal relationship` EQUALS JUST `generally, the exclusive licensing raises no antitrust concern: there is no horizontal relationship among licensors, among licensees, or between the licensor and a licensee`
-- Exclusive with a horizontal relationship: "only if" states nothing.
#ASSERT `4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`a license where` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `licensees in a horizontal relationship` EQUALS NOTHING
-- Non-exclusive with no restraint: no concern, even in a horizontal relationship.
#ASSERT `4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`a license where` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) `licensees in a horizontal relationship` EQUALS JUST `generally, the non-exclusive license does not present antitrust concerns: it contains no restraint on the competitive conduct of the licensor or the licensee`
-- Non-exclusive with a restraint, or with exclusive dealing by cost: nothing stated.
#ASSERT `4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`a license where` FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) `no horizontal relationship` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.1.2: what the agencies say of the license's exclusivity` (`a license where` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) `no horizontal relationship` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive dealing` (`a license where` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive dealing` (`a license where` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE)
-- A single licensee, a single field, a sole licensee by choice, and licensees choosing the
-- technology: none of these alone makes a license exclusive or exclusive dealing.
`a license with only the "merely because" facts` MEANS `License terms and structure (4.1.2)` OF FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE
#ASSERT NOT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive licensing` `a license with only the "merely because" facts`
#ASSERT NOT `4.1.2: the license has the effect of exclusive dealing` `a license with only the "merely because" facts`

§§ `4.2`

#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `no likely effect`, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not challenge the restraint`
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not give weight to the parties' efficiency claim`
-- Fork F23 (assumed, not ruled; revised 2026-11-25): 4.2's later steps follow the
-- conclusion that the restraint "has, or is likely to have, an anticompetitive effect".
-- With it, reasonably necessary gives the balance; with no conclusion yet, 4.2 states no
-- outcome, whatever else is found. (The earlier reading took no conclusion as a contrary
-- one, and would balance in the second case and not give weight in the third.)
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will balance the procompetitive efficiencies and the anticompetitive effects to determine the probable net effect on competition in each relevant market`
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `no conclusion yet`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `no conclusion yet`, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- Fork F16 (assumed, not ruled; revised on review 2026-11-25): a clear, significantly less
-- restrictive alternative wins over a finding of reasonable necessity: "will not give
-- weight". (The earlier reading here was NOTHING; letting necessity win would balance.)
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will not give weight to the parties' efficiency claim`
-- Likely anticompetitive, not reasonably necessary, no clear alternative: nothing stated.
#ASSERT `4.2: what the agencies do on their findings` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `4.2: the considerations against reasonable necessity that are present` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS LIST `a practical and significantly less restrictive alternative`, `a duration clearly exceeding the period needed to achieve the efficiency`
#ASSERT `4.2: the considerations against reasonable necessity that are present` (`Findings under the rule of reason` OF `a likely effect`, FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS EMPTY

§§ `5.2`

#ASSERT `5.2: price maintenance` (`Price maintenance facts (5.2)` OF FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.2: price maintenance` (`Price maintenance facts (5.2)` OF TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agreement constitutes a horizontal cartel, and will be considered per se illegal`
#ASSERT `5.2: price maintenance` (`Price maintenance facts (5.2)` OF TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis, case by case, evaluating the competitive benefits and harms`

§§ `5.3`

GIVEN tie IS A BOOLEAN
      power IS A BOOLEAN
      protected IS A BOOLEAN
      adverse IS A BOOLEAN
      outweigh IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Tying facts (5.3)`
`a tie where` MEANS `Tying facts (5.3)` OF tie, power, protected, adverse, outweigh

#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`
-- Each of the three conditions failing alone; and no tie at all. Nothing stated.
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
-- "will not presume that a patent, copyright, or trade secret necessarily confers market
-- power": protection without a finding of market power is not enough.
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.3: tying` (`a tie where` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies would be likely to challenge the tying arrangement`

§§ `5.4`

#ASSERT `5.4: exclusive dealing` (`a license where` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.4: exclusive dealing` (`a license where` FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS JUST `exclusive dealing arrangements are evaluated under the rule of reason`
#ASSERT `5.4: the matters present` (`Exclusive dealing facts (5.4)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS LIST `anticompetitive foreclosure of, or constraint on competition among, competing technologies`, `other increases in competition and output in a relevant market`

§§ `5.5`

#ASSERT `5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the arrangement is subject to challenge under the per se rule`
#ASSERT `5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`a restraint of` `naked price-fixing` FALSE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS `following section 3.4, the agencies will apply a rule of reason analysis`
-- 5.5's per se words are only for the two restraints it names (fork F25, 2026-11-25): an
-- output restraint without integration gets 3.4's words, attributed to 3.4. (Giving every
-- per se type 5.5's words would put a sentence 5.5 does not say into its mouth.)
#ASSERT `5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`a restraint of` `an output restraint` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `following section 3.4, the agencies will challenge the restraint under the per se rule`
#ASSERT `5.5: the mode of analysis of a collective restraint in a pool or cross-license` (`a restraint of` `market division among horizontal competitors` FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS `the arrangement is subject to challenge under the per se rule`

#ASSERT `5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will evaluate whether the limitations on participation are reasonably related to the efficient development and exploitation of the pooled technologies, and will assess their net effect in the relevant market`
-- "unless (1) ... and (2) ...": either missing, unlikely.
#ASSERT `5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `in general, exclusion is unlikely to have anticompetitive effects`
#ASSERT `5.5: exclusion from a pool or cross-license` (`Exclusion from a pool or cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS JUST `in general, exclusion is unlikely to have anticompetitive effects`

#ASSERT `5.5: a pool's grant of current and future technology at minimal cost` (`Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` OF TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the arrangement is not likely to cause competitive problems: it does not include a large fraction of the potential research and development in a research and development market`
#ASSERT `5.5: a pool's grant of current and future technology at minimal cost` (`Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` OF TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.5: a pool's grant of current and future technology at minimal cost` (`Pool terms on future technology (5.5)` OF FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

#ASSERT `5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the settlement may be challenged as an unlawful restraint of trade`
#ASSERT `5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.5: a settlement by cross-license` (`Settlement by cross-license (5.5)` OF FALSE, TRUE, FALSE) EQUALS NOTHING

§§ `5.6`

#ASSERT `5.6: a grantback` (`Grantback facts (5.6)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS JUST `the agencies will evaluate the grantback provision under the rule of reason`
#ASSERT `5.6: a grantback` (`Grantback facts (5.6)` OF FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `5.6: the matters present` (`Grantback facts (5.6)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS LIST `the exclusivity of the grantback`, `the licensor's market power in a relevant technology or research and development market`, `a likely significant reduction in licensees' incentives to invest in improving the licensed technology`, `promotion of the dissemination of licensees' improvements`, `greater incentives for licensors to disseminate the licensed technology`, `other increases in competition and output in a relevant technology or research and development market`, `greater incentives for licensors to innovate in the first place, from grantback provisions in the relevant markets generally`
-- Fork F12 (assumed, not ruled): the offsetting effects are considered only once the
-- agencies determine a significant reduction in incentives. Without it, they are not
-- reported. (Reporting them always would list four more.)
#ASSERT `5.6: the matters present` (`Grantback facts (5.6)` OF TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, FALSE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE, TRUE) EQUALS LIST `the exclusivity of the grantback`, `the licensor's market power in a relevant technology or research and development market`

§§ `5.7`

#ASSERT `5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF TRUE, FALSE, FALSE) EQUALS `the agencies will apply a merger analysis: an outright sale of all rights to the intellectual property`
#ASSERT `5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` (`Transfer of intellectual property rights (5.7)` OF FALSE, FALSE, TRUE) EQUALS `the agencies may also apply a merger analysis: a license that in substance transfers the rights`
#ASSERT `5.7: merger analysis of the transfer` `no transfer` EQUALS `section 5.7 calls for no merger analysis`

§§ `6`

GIVEN enforcement IS A BOOLEAN
      invalid IS A BOOLEAN
      fraud IS A BOOLEAN
      inequitable IS A BOOLEAN
      elements IS A BOOLEAN
      sham IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH AN `Enforcement of intellectual property rights (6)`
`enforcement where` MEANS `Enforcement of intellectual property rights (6)` OF enforcement, invalid, fraud, inequitable, elements, sham

-- Not enforcement: the four enforcement sentences do not speak. Inequitable conduct that is
-- also fraud with the elements: the section 2 sentence does not speak either.
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- Revised on review 2026-11-25: the inequitable-conduct sentence is about the conduct
-- before the Patent and Trademark Office, not about enforcement, so it speaks without it.
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `the inequitable conduct will not be the basis of a section 2 claim`
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the agencies may challenge the enforcement of invalid intellectual property rights as an antitrust violation`
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `it may violate section 2 of the Sherman Act or section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act`
-- Fraud, but the other elements not proved, and no inequitable conduct found: section 6
-- states nothing on it (fork F20).
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS EMPTY
-- Inequitable conduct short of fraud: not a section 2 basis; may violate section 5.
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the inequitable conduct will not be the basis of a section 2 claim`, `under some circumstances it may violate section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act`
-- Inequitable conduct that is also fraud, but the other elements are not present: "unless"
-- needs both, so it is still not a section 2 basis; and it is not short of fraud, so the
-- section 5 sentence does not speak.
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `the inequitable conduct will not be the basis of a section 2 claim`
-- Inequitable conduct that is also fraud, with the elements: the fraud sentence only.
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE FALSE) EQUALS LIST `it may violate section 2 of the Sherman Act or section 5 of the Federal Trade Commission Act`
#ASSERT `6: what section 6 says of the enforcement` (`enforcement where` TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE FALSE TRUE) EQUALS LIST `sham litigation may constitute an element of a violation of the Sherman Act`
